{
  "slug": "slipstream",
  "name": "Slipstream",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "A tool that makes AI coding agents more effective for Dart and Flutter projects.\n\nAI agents working on Dart and Flutter run into two recurring problems. First, their training data has a cutoff — they'll reach for discontinued packages, pin outdated major versions, or produce subtly wrong API signatures that compile only after a correction loop. Second, Flutter development is inherently visual and stateful, and agents have no way to see a running app: they can't observe a layout failure, verify that a state change took effect, or confirm that a navigation worked.\n\nThis tool addresses both. It adds hooks that catch stale package choices before they land in `pubspec.yaml`, an MCP server that retrieves accurate package API signatures directly from the local pub cache, and a suite of MCP commands for launching, inspecting, and interacting with a running Flutter app.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **3 skills** and **2 MCP servers**.\n\n- **Skills** (3): `add-package` (This skill should be used when about to add a Dart or Flutter package dependency — running flutter…), `slipstream-inspector` (This skill should be used when the user asks to \"run the Flutter app\", \"flutter run\", \"start the…), `slipstream-packages` (This skill should be used when about to write Dart or Flutter code that calls into a pub…)\n- **MCP servers** (2): `packages`, `inspector`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install slipstream@claude-community` from `devoncarew/flutter-slipstream`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "codex"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 3,
    "mcp": 2
  },
